(1489140, 195993, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture so easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Trees make great leading lines but yours seems to lead the viewer back out of the image again. The trees themselves appear to be the main subject.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture so easiest to pick up. Trees make great leading lines but yours seems to lead the viewer back out of the image again. The trees themselves appear to be the main subject.', '2005-06-28 18:53:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489145, 195071, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture so easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Your lines are a major element of the composition but most do not lead the viewer anywhere.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture so easiest to pick up. Your lines are a major element of the composition but most do not lead the viewer anywhere.', '2005-06-28 18:55:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489150, 196281, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture so easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>An curious twist on the concept of leading lines.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture so easiest to pick up. An curious twist on the concept of leading lines.', '2005-06-28 18:56:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489166, 195523, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture so easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>This foreground boat adds great interest to the composition and effectively leads the viewer to the background boat in the background. Very creative approach to the challenge.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture so easiest to pick up. This foreground boat adds great interest to the composition and effectively leads the viewer to the background boat in the background. Very creative approach to the challenge.', '2005-06-28 18:59:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489172, 194925, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture so easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Your leading lines from the traditional direction effectively direct the viewer to the city.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture so easiest to pick up. Your leading lines from the traditional direction effectively direct the viewer to the city.', '2005-06-28 19:00:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489176, 196347, 2170, '<td valign="top">this is a fantastic photograph</td>', 'this is a fantastic photograph', '2005-06-28 19:01:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489178, 196175, 2170, '<td valign="top">it''s got lines, but they don''t really lead me anywhere.</td>', 'it''s got lines, but they don''t really lead me anywhere.', '2005-06-28 19:01:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489179, 196224, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture so easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>The line leads nicely to the white structure but its small size and the fact that it is overexposed will not be much of a visual payoff for most voters.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture so easiest to pick up. The line leads nicely to the white structure but its small size and the fact that it is overexposed will not be much of a visual payoff for most voters.', '2005-06-28 19:02:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489181, 196114, 2170, '<td valign="top">this is gorgeous and very well-executed.  perfect for this challenge.</td>', 'this is gorgeous and very well-executed.  perfect for this challenge.', '2005-06-28 19:02:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489186, 195820, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Your have nice lines leading to the boater but not to the skyline that takes up most of the frame.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. Your have nice lines leading to the boater but not to the skyline that takes up most of the frame.', '2005-06-28 19:04:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489188, 194777, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>The lines effectively lead the viewer to the distant farmhouse but some voters may not feel that is the main subject.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. The lines effectively lead the viewer to the distant farmhouse but some voters may not feel that is the main subject.', '2005-06-28 19:05:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489190, 196289, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Very creative and effective way to direct attention to the birds.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. Very creative and effective way to direct attention to the birds.', '2005-06-28 19:06:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489196, 196274, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Some images do not have to fit the traditional rules to work and be effective. In your case the lines themselves make for a wonderful abstract composition.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. Some images do not have to fit the traditional rules to work and be effective. In your case the lines themselves make for a wonderful abstract composition.', '2005-06-28 19:08:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489198, 195623, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Curved rails on a track make very nice leading lines.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. Curved rails on a track make very nice leading lines.', '2005-06-28 19:09:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489202, 195679, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>You lines do a great job of pointing out to the viewer that this is a stark and very open lake.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. You lines do a great job of pointing out to the viewer that this is a stark and very open lake.', '2005-06-28 19:11:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489205, 196171, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Nice lines that make the viewer wonder what is on the trail beyond the bridge.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. Nice lines that make the viewer wonder what is on the trail beyond the bridge.', '2005-06-28 19:12:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489207, 196399, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Stairwells are very effective at directing attention. Good thought.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. Stairwells are very effective at directing attention. Good thought.', '2005-06-28 19:13:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489213, 195679, 37529, '<td valign="top">Excellent photo for this challenge.  Good composition and color is refreshing and focused.</td>', 'Excellent photo for this challenge.  Good composition and color is refreshing and focused.', '2005-06-28 19:17:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489214, 195774, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Focus is also an effective way to direct attention to the main subject. In this case the image is nice but the viewer may be confused where you want them to look. You might consider shooting this with focus set to infinity. That way the leading lines and focus directs the viewer to the same place.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. Focus is also an effective way to direct attention to the main subject. In this case the image is nice but the viewer may be confused where you want them to look. You might consider shooting this with focus set to infinity. That way the leading lines and focus directs the viewer to the same place.', '2005-06-28 19:17:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489223, 195792, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Attention is drawn to both the opening in the clouds which is into the scene AND the silhouetted horizon.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. Attention is drawn to both the opening in the clouds which is into the scene AND the silhouetted horizon.', '2005-06-28 19:21:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489224, 196288, 38592, '<td valign="top">I can see where you were going with the bench lines leading to the lady, but personally I just see a girl sitting there.  I think to place hign in the challenge the lines are going to have ben very dominant in the image.  I think what takes away from the line the most is the break in between the two benches.</td>', 'I can see where you were going with the bench lines leading to the lady, but personally I just see a girl sitting there.  I think to place hign in the challenge the lines are going to have ben very dominant in the image.  I think what takes away from the line the most is the break in between the two benches.', '2005-06-28 19:21:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489225, 194252, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Classic example of leading lines. Great capture!</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. Classic example of leading lines. Great capture!', '2005-06-28 19:22:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489226, 196102, 27763, '<td valign="top">This totally rocks!  I love it!</td>', 'This totally rocks!  I love it!', '2005-06-28 19:22:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489227, 196199, 38592, '<td valign="top">I love this idea.  Great image however my personal preference would have been to have the entire image in focus as the crumb sharpness fades (probably by choice I realize).  Still gets a high rating from me.</td>', 'I love this idea.  Great image however my personal preference would have been to have the entire image in focus as the crumb sharpness fades (probably by choice I realize).  Still gets a high rating from me.', '2005-06-28 19:23:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489229, 196279, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>The barbed wire appears to be the main subject itself and does not lead the viewer to any one place in the frame.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. The barbed wire appears to be the main subject itself and does not lead the viewer to any one place in the frame.', '2005-06-28 19:23:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1489234, 196373, 5792, '<td valign="top">Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up.<br/> <br/>Good thought from the classic direction. This leads in one direction but does not have a visual payoff at the end. Some voters might vote it lower because of that.</td>', 'Leading lines or curves generally have two purposes. One is to lead the viewer into the scene. The other is to lead you toward the main subject. It is most effective if they come in from the lower left because that is the natural direction humans visually scan a picture from so are easiest to pick up. Good thought from the classic direction. This leads in one direction but does not have a visual payoff at the end. Some voters might vote it lower because of that.', '2005-06-28 19:26:17.000000', NULL, 1),
