(1501172, 195910, 31175, '<td valign="top">Super shot. Lovely composition.</td>', 'Super shot. Lovely composition.', '2005-07-03 03:08:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1501173, 196114, 19831, '<td valign="top">Wowsers. To me this is an incredibly awesome shot. Technically, focus and everything is great. The composition and the overall concept blows me away. Catching the reflections in the floor is really cool. I love the placement of the person. Great perspective, and with the light, really tells the story. Great example of ''leading lines'' IMO. Great title. I just really like this image. Wonderful job. thanks.</td>', 'Wowsers. To me this is an incredibly awesome shot. Technically, focus and everything is great. The composition and the overall concept blows me away. Catching the reflections in the floor is really cool. I love the placement of the person. Great perspective, and with the light, really tells the story. Great example of ''leading lines'' IMO. Great title. I just really like this image. Wonderful job. thanks.', '2005-07-03 03:08:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1501174, 196236, 31175, '<td valign="top">Too limited a colour range for me.</td>', 'Too limited a colour range for me.', '2005-07-03 03:12:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1501176, 195828, 19831, '<td valign="top">Nice image. Great texture in the shot. Beautiful composition. Great exposure. Good interest factor. Nice job.</td>', 'Nice image. Great texture in the shot. Beautiful composition. Great exposure. Good interest factor. Nice job.', '2005-07-03 03:15:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1501185, 195956, 19831, '<td valign="top">Good concept. Fits the challenge IMO. Nice sunset. I like how the vanishing point of the towers goes into the heart of the sunset. Maybe it''s just me, but I''m thinking this photo could be a little stronger with a slightly different framing/cropping. The top part to me seems a little weak. What I see is these nice lines from the wires, but then the way the 2 main wires go out one at the top and one appears in this perspective to go out the side. Also, I get a slightly unbalanced feel between the black at the bottom, the lovely golds in the middle, and then a lot of blue/gray at the top. I''m thinking that maybe cropping it to just a little above the top of the tower, that it would provide a little ''symmetry'' , where there would be a little bit of black at bottom, lots of gold in the middle highlighting the main subject, then a little bit of blue/gray. Also giving a more flowing, continual feel to the lines of the wires. Just my opinion :-)</td>', 'Good concept. Fits the challenge IMO. Nice sunset. I like how the vanishing point of the towers goes into the heart of the sunset. Maybe it''s just me, but I''m thinking this photo could be a little stronger with a slightly different framing/cropping. The top part to me seems a little weak. What I see is these nice lines from the wires, but then the way the 2 main wires go out one at the top and one appears in this perspective to go out the side. Also, I get a slightly unbalanced feel between the black at the bottom, the lovely golds in the middle, and then a lot of blue/gray at the top. I''m thinking that maybe cropping it to just a little above the top of the tower, that it would provide a little ''symmetry'' , where there would be a little bit of black at bottom, lots of gold in the middle highlighting the main subject, then a little bit of blue/gray. Also giving a more flowing, continual feel to the lines of the wires. Just my opinion :-)', '2005-07-03 03:31:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1501189, 196093, 32602, '<td valign="top">Powerlines are not usually nice to look at in real life, but here they are like a necklace strung across the countryside right to the horizon, it''s a good shot.</td>', 'Powerlines are not usually nice to look at in real life, but here they are like a necklace strung across the countryside right to the horizon, it''s a good shot.', '2005-07-03 03:36:09.000000', NULL, 1),
