(4923500, 196271, 54645, '<td valign="top">What an interesting image. Well done. I wonder...if you were not shooting for the challenge, your main point of focus could have been further in to the image. I love the contrast between a water tower and cactus.</td>', 'What an interesting image. Well done. I wonder...if you were not shooting for the challenge, your main point of focus could have been further in to the image. I love the contrast between a water tower and cactus.', '2008-08-31 19:54:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5117082, 196271, 73942, '<td valign="top">I love the leading lines of a railroad track shot, but this one has even more with the bend in the tracks. I think making this B&amp;W adds even more.</td>', 'I love the leading lines of a railroad track shot, but this one has even more with the bend in the tracks. I think making this B&W adds even more.', '2008-12-08 12:08:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6116261, 195282, 40718, '<td valign="top">I''m enjoying looking through people''s portfolios.  I''ve often started with a 5.5 score because it generally means promise that wasn''t fulfilled.  A few things grab me with this shot.  First, you have found a nice leading line, but the problem is it doesn''t lead to anywhere.  If anything, it leads to that clump of bush which is very unexciting for us.  I''m glad to see you used a polarizer.  You may have wanted to try to saturated or darken the sky a bit more in processing.  Sometimes you can set a new layer to multiply and then provide a gradient down the sky.  That can look very nice.  The gold does contrast nicely with the blue.</td>', 'I''m enjoying looking through people''s portfolios.  I''ve often started with a 5.5 score because it generally means promise that wasn''t fulfilled.  A few things grab me with this shot.  First, you have found a nice leading line, but the problem is it doesn''t lead to anywhere.  If anything, it leads to that clump of bush which is very unexciting for us.  I''m glad to see you used a polarizer.  You may have wanted to try to saturated or darken the sky a bit more in processing.  Sometimes you can set a new layer to multiply and then provide a gradient down the sky.  That can look very nice.  The gold does contrast nicely with the blue.', '2010-08-03 22:58:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(6929370, 195588, 97225, '<td valign="top">Wow, I''m so glad this oldie has been drawn to my attention. Fabulous colour and pattern.</td>', 'Wow, I''m so glad this oldie has been drawn to my attention. Fabulous colour and pattern.', '2012-12-10 18:52:44.000000', NULL, 0),
